course: dictionary
lesson: 4992
title: Colour words and the rainbow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a colour, and some name a colour that sits between two others. Indigo is one of these. It is a deep blue-purple, and it is one of the seven colours of the rainbow. «Its colours are always in the same order: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet.» Indigo comes after blue and before violet.
explain: Indigo is also a dark blue dye, the colour used on cloth such as jeans. «Jeans are dyed with indigo» means the jeans get their colour from this dye. Ask yourself: is the word talking about a colour in a rainbow, or a dye for cloth? The words around it give the clue.
explain: Lists of colours help you place a new word. «The colours of the rainbow are red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet, with red on the outside edge of the bow.» If you know blue and violet, you can find indigo between them.
fact: Indigo is one of the seven colours of the rainbow.
fact: Indigo sits between blue and violet in the rainbow.
fact: Indigo is a deep blue-purple colour, and as a dye it makes a dark blue.
fact: «Indigo» was once made from plants; now it is usually made in factories.
fact: The rainbow's colours always come in the same order, with red on the outside edge of the bow.
exercise: What colour sits between blue and violet in the rainbow? | Green | Yellow | *Indigo | Orange
exercise: «Jeans are dyed with indigo.» What is indigo used for here? | *To colour cloth | To make rain fall | To make a rainbow in the sky | To make a bright red sun
exercise: Which list gives the rainbow colours in the right order? | Green, yellow, indigo, red, violet, orange, blue | Indigo, red, green, violet, blue, orange, yellow | Violet, blue, red, yellow, orange, green, indigo | *Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet
test: «The first indigo blue for jeans came from a plant.» Where did the first indigo come from? | A river | A rainbow | *A plant | A factory
test: Which colour comes straight after indigo in the rainbow? | Blue | Orange | *Violet | Green
exam: What is indigo? | A type of rain | A kind of fruit | A large bird | *A deep blue-purple colour
